    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, the Austin Waves offense is anchored by **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) and **Kyle Tucker** (71.28), our clear-cut top plays. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from an exceptional matchup against Pecko, whose 5.95 xERA suggests a volatile outing, further aided by a +19% SP skill adjustment and a favorable platoon edge. **Kyle Tucker** remains a plug-and-play elite option; despite facing Elder, his floor remains high due to consistent power output and a solid +9% SP skill advantage. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (69.26) also provides significant upside against Lugo, utilizing a strong park factor and favorable pitching matchup to climb near the 70-point threshold despite a slight platoon dip.\n\nStrategic optimization was tested at the utility and bench spots. **Miguel Vargas** (39.60) was the primary casualty, falling just shy of our 40-point \"start\" threshold. While his xwOBA of 0.389 remains promising, he was suppressed by a tough draw against deGrom and our internal \"Zebras Floor\" mandate, which prioritized benching him to preserve precious game caps. Meanwhile, our lineup remains hampered by the absence of core contributors **Jordan Westburg**, **Andy Pages**, and **Jacob Wilson**, all currently stashed on the IL. We are closely monitoring the status of **Heliot Ramos**, **Josh Jung**, **Dominic Smith**, **Curtis Mead**, **Wade Meckler**, **Luis Lara**, and **Tommy White** for potential depth support as we navigate these remaining games.\n\nRisk management is paramount today given the high-end opposing talent. **Jackson Merrill** (48.97) and **Sam Antonacci** (46.73) face the daunting challenge of deGrom and Skenes, respectively; while both possess enough projectable value to start, their scores are heavily suppressed by elite SP skill adjustments and defensive efficiency\u2014specifically against stolen base attempts. **Gunnar Henderson** (53.04) and **Coby Mayo** (53.15) draw a respectable matchup against Liberatore, but managers should expect a defensive grind. As we chase the league-wide scarcity of stolen bases, we have opted to keep **Nasim Nunez** in the lineup (41.15) despite his lower score, prioritizing his elite speed profile to stay competitive in our most critical category.",
